course: dictionary
lesson: 15916
title: Unpalatable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unpalatable means unpleasant to taste, or hard to accept. The word starts with «un», which means not, and palatable means pleasant to taste. So unpalatable means not pleasant to taste.
explain: «The soup was cold, salty and burnt, so it was unpalatable.» Nobody wants to eat soup like that. The clues are cold, salty and burnt, so unpalatable must mean nasty to eat or drink.
explain: The word can also describe ideas and facts. «The unpalatable truth was that the trip had been cancelled.» Nobody likes to hear this news, so the truth is hard to accept. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «hard to accept» still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Unpalatable means unpleasant to taste, or hard to accept.
fact: The «un» at the start means not, and «palatable» means pleasant to taste.
fact: «Unpalatable» can describe food or drink that tastes nasty.
fact: «The unpalatable truth» means a fact that people do not want to hear.
fact: Some insects taste unpalatable, so birds learn not to eat them. Bright colours can warn birds to stay away.
exercise: «The milk had gone sour and tasted unpalatable.» What does unpalatable mean? | *Unpleasant to taste | Easy to find | Sweet and creamy | Cold and fizzy
exercise: «The unpalatable truth was that the match had been cancelled.» What does unpalatable describe? | Bright and colourful | Very tasty | *Hard to accept or hear | Very loud
exercise: Why do birds learn not to eat some bright insects? | Birds cannot see bright colours | The insects are too big to swallow | The insects sing loudly | *Those insects taste unpalatable
test: «The leaders faced an unpalatable choice: close the library or close the swimming pool.» What does unpalatable mean in this sentence? | Quick and easy | Bright and colourful | *Hard and unpleasant to accept | Tasty and cheap
test: What does the «un» at the start of unpalatable mean? | Very | Before | Again | *Not
exam: «Everyone agreed it was an unpalatable truth, but Mia still said it out loud.» What is the best meaning of unpalatable here? | *Hard to hear or accept | Pleasant to hear | Funny and surprising | Sweet and tasty
